# =============================================================================
# yard.dlg  -  The test yard's street: two shopkeepers and a closed sign
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Format: systems/dialogue/dialogue_script.gd (header). Speakers are
# data/characters/<ID>.tres. Used by realms/big_yard/prototype_yard.gd
# (SHOPS_BY_CHAR): a shop plays its greet node and then hands over its item
# once per phase of the game clock; after that, the "again" node. Tech demo
# lines, not story.
#
# Written with help from Claude (Anthropic) via Claude Code.
# Made with love from your friendly hacker - er2oneousbit
# =============================================================================

== shop_corner
GROCER: Morning, noon or golden hour, the corner store's open. Here, take an apple.
GROCER: No money? Nobody has money. We close when it gets dark.

== shop_corner_again
GROCER: That's your apple for now. Come back later and there might be another.

== shop_corner_closed
: CLOSED. Open again in the morning.

== shop_allnight
VENDOR: Open all night, every night. Have a soda, on the house.

== shop_allnight_again
VENDOR: One per customer per shift. I don't make the rules. I do, actually.
